# THE REFERENCE SURFACE — the one declaration of "what it means for a test to be
# referenced" (order 1325-ygq5).
#
# A test is DONE when something that runs on its own can fail because of it.
# This file names the things that "run on their own". It exists because the
# packet's own unscoreable said the surface was four places and declared in
# none: a fifth caller added tomorrow would make a referenced test look
# unreferenced, and the guard would start naming innocent files. Now adding a
# caller means adding a line here, and the verdict line carries the surface
# count so a reader can see when it changes.
#
# Format: <organ> <path-or-glob>
#   shell   — searched for the BASENAME of an added scripts/test-*.sh
#   litmus  — searched for the declared `name:` of an added litmus yaml
#
# Globs are expanded by the guard, not by a shell at read time; a pattern that
# matches nothing is reported, never silently skipped (that silence is the
# whole failure shape this packet is about).

shell   scripts/gate-steps.d/*.step
shell   build.sh
shell   scripts/local-ci.sh
shell   scripts/hooks/*.sh
shell   openspec/litmus-tests/*.yaml

litmus  openspec/litmus-bindings.yaml
